<title>FINLAND: FORECAST-AAMULEHTI 4-MTH PROFIT SEEN UP.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-AAMULEHTI 4-MTH PROFIT SEEN UP.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Reuters survey of analysts</p>
<p>covering Finnish equities showed a 43 million markka median</p>
<p>forecast for Finnish media group Aamulehti Oy's January-April</p>
<p>profit before extraordinary items and tax.</p>
<p>		     Profit before extras, tax</p>
<p>			   (FIM million)</p>
<p>    Median		    43</p>
<p>    Mean			44</p>
<p>    Lowest		    33</p>
<p>    Highest		   55</p>
<p>(Forecasts by nine analysts).</p>
<p>Aamulehti's results are due on June 6 around 1200/0900 GMT.</p>
<p>In January-April 1996, Aamulehti posted a profit of 32</p>
<p>million markka.</p>
<p>Contributors to the survey were Alfred Berg, AG Private</p>
<p>Bankers, Aktia Bank, Aros Securities, Carnegie Securities, Erik</p>
<p>Selin, Evli Securities, Merita Securities, Opstock Securities</p>
<p>and Postipankki.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom 358-9-680 50 292, news@reuters.fi</p>
